# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Binary loader/driver payloads shipped verbatim to the memory card: the POPSTARTER assets plus the
# BDMAssault IRX variants. NEVER line-ending normalize these -- a stray CRLF<->LF pass corrupts the
# IRX and POPSTARTER then fails to load it.
#
# BOTH lines are needed, and the directory rule is spelled POPS/ on purpose. The BDMAssault variants
# are named usbd.irx.ata / usbhdfsd.irx.mmce / ... -- the extension is the MODE, so they do NOT end
# in ".irx" and `*.irx` alone misses every one of them. Upstream spells this rule `pops/*`, which
# matches nothing on a case-sensitive checkout (the directory is POPS/), so the CI runner never
# applied it; using the real casing here is a deliberate divergence, not a typo.
#
# Spelled `POPS/**` rather than `POPS/*` because the folder now carries a "POPSTARTER VERSIONS"
# subdirectory of alternate POPSTARTER builds, and the single-star form stops at the top level --
# exactly the reason EMBER/** below is spelled the same way. Those nested files are PS2 ELFs; a
# CRLF<->LF pass through one produces a binary that no longer loads, and the failure would surface
# as "this POPSTARTER variant hangs" long after the commit that caused it.
POPS/** binary
*.irx binary

# Ember's core, shipped verbatim exactly like the POPSTARTER payload above. ember.elf is a PS2 ELF;
# a CRLF<->LF pass through it produces a binary that no longer loads, and the failure would show up
# as "Ember does not start" long after the commit that caused it.
#
# Spelled with ** rather than EMBER/* because the folder carries a games/ subdirectory, and the
# single-star form stops at the top level. The `*.url text eol=crlf` rule further down deliberately
# still wins for EMBER/Ember Official Webpage.url -- gitattributes is last-match-wins, and a Windows
# internet shortcut is one of the few files that genuinely must check out with CRLF.
EMBER/** binary

# Internet shortcuts are a Windows-native format and must check out with CRLF. pc/PS2-Servers.url is
# copied straight into the release package, so this is load-bearing at publish time, not cosmetic.
*.url text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts check out with LF even on Windows.
#
# `* text=auto` above already STORES them as LF, so this changes nothing in history -- only what
# lands on disk. Without it a Windows checkout writes CRLF, and every containerised build then has
# to run dos2unix over the tree (a CRLF shebang reads as `#!/bin/bash\r` and dies with a bare
# "No such file or directory" / Error 127). That rewrite dirties ten tracked scripts on every
# build, so `git status` is never clean, real edits hide among the noise, and the line-ending
# churn keeps getting committed by accident.
#
# Nothing on Windows needs a CRLF .sh: these run under Git Bash, WSL or the ps2dev container, all
# of which want LF.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Custom for Visual Studio
*.cs   diff=csharp

# Standard to msysgit
*.doc  diff=astextplain
*.DOC  diff=astextplain
*.docx diff=astextplain
*.DOCX diff=astextplain
*.dot  diff=astextplain
*.DOT  diff=astextplain
*.pdf  diff=astextplain
*.PDF  diff=astextplain
*.rtf  diff=astextplain
*.RTF  diff=astextplain
